    buf = bytearray()
    for chunk in chunks:
        if not chunk:
            continue
        buf += chunk
        start = 0
        while True:
            i = buf.find(b'\n', start)
            if i == -1:
                break
            end = i
            if end > start and buf[end - 1] == 0x0D:
                end -= 1
            yield buf[start:end].decode('utf-8')
            start = i + 1
        if start:
            del buf[:start]
    if buf:
        yield buf.decode('utf-8')
", "explanation": "Bytes are accumulated in a buffer; complete LF-terminated segments are decoded and yielded incrementally, so UTF-8 decoding naturally spans chunks (only whole lines are decoded once their bytes are complete). Exactly one CR immediately before LF is stripped; a bare CR not followed by LF (like in 'B\rC\n') is preserved. Empty chunks are skipped, not treated as EOF. At EOF a nonempty residual buffer is decoded strictly; incomplete UTF-8 (b'\xf0\x9f') raises UnicodeDecodeError after prior lines were already yielded. No extra empty line is emitted after a terminal LF since the buffer is empty. Memory bound: O(max line length + one incomplete UTF-8 sequence), never the whole input. Limitation: a lone CR at a chunk boundary followed by LF in the next chunk is correctly stripped because splitting happens on the accumulated buffer, not per chunk."}
